step: The keys of every step.

A step is a map. It has one module key, such as pkg or file, with the
arguments of the module as a map. Or it has recipe with the name of a
recipe. Run winch doc <module> for the arguments of a module.

```yaml
# winch.yaml
name: demo
hosts:
  web1.example.com: {}
vars:
  sites: [blog, shop]
steps:
  - name: Install nginx
    pkg:
      name: nginx
  - name: Write the sites
    file:
      path: !tpl /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/{{ .item }}.conf
      content: !tpl "# {{ .item }}\n"
    when: !expr len(vars.sites) > 0
    loop: !expr vars.sites
    then: nginx -t
    notify: reload
handlers:
  reload:
    - service:
        name: nginx
        reloaded: true
```

On each host, winch evaluates when. When it is false, winch skips the
step. Then winch evaluates loop, and the arguments for each element.
The helper checks the step on the host, and apply changes what differs.

A step that runs a command counts as changed: a cmd, and a service with
restarted or reloaded. When a step fails, its host stops; other hosts
go on.

winch fmt puts the step keys in this order: name, the module or
recipe, vars, when, loop, then, confirm_access, notify.

Keys:
  name            string                     -      Text for the plan and the logs.
  recipe          string                     -      The recipe that the step runs, in place of a module.
  vars            map                        -      Values of variables for this recipe step only.
  when            expression                 -      An !expr that gives true or false.
  loop            list or expression         -      A list, or an !expr that gives a list.
  then            string                     -      A command.
  confirm_access  boolean                    false  Check that a new SSH connection works after the step, and put back the files of the recipe when it does not.
  notify          string or list of strings  -      A handler name, or a list of them.

Run "winch doc step.<key>" for the full text of a key.
